# Error Documentation

## Part A — Portfolio (this project)

### A1. Node 16 has no stable `node:test`

- **Context**: `node --version` is v16.16.0; `node:test` landed in 16.17/18.
- **Symptom**: `node --test` fails with `bad option: --test`.
- **Resolution**: Shared assert-based harness at `test/lib/test-runner.js`, suites run
  through `test/run-all.js` (`npm test`), which exits non-zero on any failure.
- **State**: Resolved. Revisit only if the toolchain moves to Node 18+.

### A2. UMD module depending on another UMD module

- **Context**: `utils/project-data.js` needs `resume-data.js` for role provenance.
- **Symptom**: Reaching for `globalThis` inside the factory argument list resolves
  the wrong `this` and yields `undefined` in the browser.
- **Resolution**: Pass the dependency in from the wrapper body, choosing
  `require('./resume-data.js')` under CommonJS and `root.ResumeData` in the browser.
  In HTML, load `resume-data.js` **before** `project-data.js`.
- **State**: Resolved. Apply the same shape to any future cross-module util.

### A3. JS-dependent CSS can blank the page for no-JS visitors

- **Context**: `.pf-reveal` starts at `opacity: 0` for the scroll animation, and the
  mobile nav list is hidden when collapsed.
- **Symptom**: With JavaScript disabled, hidden content would never be revealed.
- **Resolution**: `theme-init.js` adds `.pf-js` to `<html>`, and every hiding rule is
  scoped under `.pf-js`. No JS means nothing is hidden.
- **State**: Resolved. Never write a hiding rule that is not gated by `.pf-js`.

### A4. Filtered items never fade in

- **Context**: Filter chips toggle `hidden` on cards that also carry `.pf-reveal`.
- **Symptom**: An item hidden before its IntersectionObserver callback fires stays at
  `opacity: 0` after being un-hidden, so it appears blank.
- **Resolution**: `index.js` and `projects.js` add `is-visible` to every item
  when a filter is applied, independent of the observer.
- **State**: Resolved.

### A4b. A filtered grid spans the wrong card

- **Context**: `pf-grid--2` spans a trailing card at an odd index across both
  columns so it is not stranded alone.
- **Symptom**: CSS `:last-child` counts cards hidden by the filter, so after
  filtering the span landed on an invisible card while a visible one sat alone.
- **Resolution**: `projects.js` adds `.is-last-visible` to the real trailing card
  when the match count is odd; a `:has()` rule makes the static selector yield.
- **State**: Resolved.

### A4c. The `hidden` attribute does nothing on a `.pf-btn`

- **Context**: The earlier-roles toggle ships with `hidden` so no-JS readers never
  see a dead control.
- **Symptom**: It rendered anyway. `.pf-btn` sets `display: inline-flex`, and an
  author-level `display` beats the UA rule behind the `hidden` attribute.
- **Resolution**: `.home-timeline__more [hidden] { display: none; }` in
  `pages/index/css/index.css`.
- **State**: Resolved. Any component with an explicit `display` needs this guard
  before `hidden` can be trusted.

### A4d. The last section could never become active in the section nav

- **Context**: `resolveActiveSection` marks a section active once its top edge
  passes the sticky chrome.
- **Symptom**: A short trailing section sits close enough to the page bottom that
  its top never clears the offset, so the link never lit up.
- **Resolution**: `resolveActiveSection` takes an `atBottom` flag and returns the
  last section when the page cannot scroll further. Covered by
  `test/home-sections.test.js`.
- **State**: Resolved.

### A4e. A hand-written tenure contradicted its own date range

- **Context**: Role dates and duration are both typed into `index.html`, while
  `resume-data.js` can derive the duration from the structured start and end.
- **Symptom**: The Playables role read "1 yr 9 mo" beside "Oct 2025 – Jul 2026",
  which is 9 months.
- **Resolution**: Corrected the markup and added an assertion comparing every
  rendered duration with `Resume.formatDuration(role.start, role.end)`.
- **State**: Resolved. Any figure derivable from the data modules should be
  compared against them in `page-markup.test.js`.

### A4f. Two filters on one page fought over the same hook

- **Context**: Folding the pages together put the work grid's filter and the
  timeline's filter in the same document. Both were written as standalone page
  scripts using `document.querySelector('[data-filter-chips]')`.
- **Symptom**: Latent, and caught before it shipped: the work section appears
  first, so the timeline would have rendered its chips into the work grid's chip
  host and left its own empty.
- **Resolution**: Each script resolves its hooks inside its own container
  (`[data-experience-filter]` / `[data-project-filter]`), and
  `test/page-markup.test.js` fails if a document-wide lookup returns.
- **State**: Resolved. When markup moves onto a shared page, re-read every
  `document.querySelector` in the scripts that came with it.

### A5. Duplicated header and footer markup across pages

- **Context**: With no build step, the nav block was repeated in every page.
- **Symptom**: Editing the nav in four of five pages was silent and easy to miss.
- **Resolution**: `test/page-markup.test.js` asserted every page carried every nav
  entry with the exact `data-nav-key` and `href`. The single-page rewrite removed
  the cause: the header and footer now exist once.
- **State**: Resolved by Milestone 5.

### A6. Root-absolute paths do not work over `file://`

- **Context**: All references use `/pages/...`, `/utils/...`, `/media/...`.
- **Symptom**: Opening `index.html` by double-clicking renders unstyled HTML.
- **Resolution**: Always preview through a server from the repository root
  (`npm start` or `python3 -m http.server`). Documented in `README.md`.
- **State**: Expected behaviour, not a bug — but it surprises people, so it is noted.

### A7. Scarlet is unreadable as text on a dark background

- **Context**: Ohio State scarlet `#ba0c2f` applied as the accent in both themes.
- **Symptom**: 2.67:1 against dark ink — below the 4.5:1 AA text minimum and below
  the 3:1 non-text minimum for a button boundary.
- **Resolution**: Split the token. `--pf-accent` is a scarlet tint (`#ff8a9c`,
  7.86:1) for dark-mode text; `--pf-accent-solid` stays scarlet for filled controls
  with white text (6.6:1); dark-mode primary buttons get an
  `--pf-accent-solid-border` tint so the boundary is identifiable.
- **State**: Resolved and locked by `test/color-contrast.test.js`.

### A8. Contrast contract too strict on decorative borders

- **Context**: An early audit required 3:1 for every border token.
- **Symptom**: Card hairlines failed, pushing the design toward heavy outlines.
- **Resolution**: WCAG 1.4.11 covers boundaries that *identify a control*, not
  decorative dividers. `--pf-border` is decorative and exempt; `--pf-border-strong`
  marks controls and is asserted at 3:1 against both the page and card surfaces
  (which forced light mode down to `gray-dark-40`, since `gray-dark-20` was 2.89:1).
- **State**: Resolved.

### A9. `auto-fit` grids orphan the last card

- **Context**: The home page's four featured cards used `pf-grid--2`
  (`auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 20rem), 1fr)`).
- **Symptom**: At container width three cards fit per row, leaving a lone fourth.
- **Resolution**: `.pf-grid--2` pins `repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr))` above 700px for
  every card grid on the site, not just the home page.
  When a fixed card count needs a fixed shape, do not use `auto-fit`.
- **State**: Resolved and asserted in `test/page-markup.test.js`.

### A10. No linting for a zero-build project

- **Context**: A stray newline inside a `.pf-visually-hidden` declaration produced an
  invalid property that no tool flagged.
- **Symptom**: Silently dropped CSS rule.
- **Resolution**: Caught by review. An HTML/CSS validator step in `npm test` is a P3
  backlog item; until then, changed CSS gets read back before commit.
- **State**: Open (low severity, backlog item).

## Part B — Inherited from the sibling `PersonalWebsite` project

Kept because the lessons still apply to any static site in this workspace.

### B1. Audio file with a space in its name fails to load

- **Resolution**: Kebab-case media filenames; `%20` encoding if a space is unavoidable.

### B2. Sticky mini-player covers the footer

- **Resolution**: Add body padding while the player is expanded; collapse to a corner
  chip when minimised.

### B3. Uneven card heights in media grids

- **Resolution**: Grid `align-items: stretch`, cards `height: 100%` with
  `display: flex; flex-direction: column`, media region `flex: 1`.

### B4. Tailwind body utilities hide a shared background image

- **Resolution**: Keep the backdrop only in `theme.css`; never put `bg-*` utilities
  on `<body>`. (Not applicable here — this project ships no Tailwind.)
